      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect. The wiki has a direct answer to this question.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **Never storing the key in the Hub\u0027s environment** \u2014 the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\n2. **Using a local secrets loader** \u2014 at startup, a secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file.\n\n3. **Injecting into child processes only** \u2014 the key is injected directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest or Query agent child process, immediately before that process starts.\n\n4. **Short-lived isolation** \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThis design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential by inspecting environment variables \u2014 since the key never exists in the Hub\u0027s own process environment, there\u0027s nothing there to leak.",
      "input_tokens": 4303,
      "output_tokens": 219
    }
